# AHK runtime

Production runtime is **AutoHotkey v1.1** (`#Requires AutoHotKey v1.1.34.04+`). Keep v1 releasable while any v2 work is side-by-side.

## Reliability

- Hotkey registration order matters (custom context → default → app profiles)
- Clean up temporary slice hotkeys after the menu closes
- Prefer process-specific launch detection over matching generic `AutoHotkey`
- Align DPI awareness; avoid full `Reload` for display changes when targeted reinit works
- Keep geometry/helpers shared with JS tests when extracting pure functions

## Naming

Use one spelling for globals (e.g. `IsStandAlone`). Fix typos instead of adding aliases that diverge.

## Actions

Dispatch built-ins through an explicit registry over time. Custom functions that run user AHK are a trust boundary — validate before write/execute.
